// @error is a compiler intrinsic and cannot be redefined
// The NARROW store widths are emitter-intercepted from the day they were declared,
// so a user definition of one of the names is reserved — the same rule the other
// sixteen lowered memory intrinsics follow.
//
// This cell differs from `store-width-user-definition-reserved.vl` in one respect
// worth writing down: that file records a behaviour that CHANGED, because
// `__store_f64__` spent a release declared-but-unlowered and genuinely shadowable.
// `__store_i8__` and `__store_i16__` were declared and lowered in the SAME change,
// so they never had a shadowing hatch to close and this reject is their first and
// only behaviour. Declaring a name before it lowers is what creates that window;
// not doing it is why there is nothing to migrate here.
function __store_i8__(a: i32, v: i32) {
  0
}
__store_i8__(0, 1)
print(1)
